From: TDVP Platform <platform@tdvp.invalid>
Date: Thu, 28 Aug 2026 16:20:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] netman: retain Raspberry Pi's shared panel ABI

The upstream wf-panel-pi C++ adapter calls the same C implementation as the
LXPanel module.  Its NMApplet instance therefore requires the fields and
callbacks selected by LXPANEL_PLUGIN, even though this product does not build
or ship the LXPanel module itself.

Keep that established shared ABI for the Wayland module.  The associated
lp-connection-editor executable contract is supplied by the product's small
compatibility launcher, which delegates to the upstream nm-connection-editor
binary.

Signed-off-by: TDVP Platform <platform@tdvp.invalid>
---
 src/applet.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/applet.h b/src/applet.h
index a22619f..9f469e1 100644
--- a/src/applet.h
+++ b/src/applet.h
@@ -31,7 +31,7 @@
 #include <libmm-glib.h>
 #endif
 
-#define LXPANEL_PLUGIN
+#define LXPANEL_PLUGIN /* shared by the wf-panel-pi adapter */
 #ifdef LXPANEL_PLUGIN
 #ifdef LXPLUG
 #include "plugin.h"
-- 
2.47.3
